.* WRKRPYLE: the system reply list's entries with their options.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SEQCL BASETYPE='ZONED 5 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=IDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 7'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=RPYCL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=CMPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 30'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STARTCL BASETYPE='ZONED 4 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LONGCL BASETYPE='CHAR 32'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=DUMPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 4'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=SEQ CLASS=SEQCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGID CLASS=IDCL.
:VAR NAME=RPY CLASS=RPYCL.
:VAR NAME=CMPDTA CLASS=CMPCL.
:VAR NAME=START CLASS=STARTCL.
:VAR NAME=RPYLONG CLASS=LONGCL.
:VAR NAME=DUMP CLASS=DUMPCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=RPYS VARS='OPT SEQ MSGID RPY CMPDTA START RPYLONG DUMP'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='CMD ?ADDRPYLE'.F6=Add
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display entire reply
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKRPYLE KEYL=KEYS HELP=WRKRPYLH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with System Reply List Entries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=RPYS VIEWS=2 SCROLL=YES.
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGRPYLE SEQNBR(&SEQ.)' HELP='WRKRPYLE/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?RMVRPYLE SEQNBR(&SEQ.)' HELP='WRKRPYLE/OPTIONS'.4=Delete
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKRPYLE/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SEQ USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SEQ'.Sequence Number
:LISTCOL VAR=MSGID USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/MSGID'.Message ID
:LISTCOL VAR=RPY USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/RPY'.Reply
:LISTCOL VAR=CMPDTA USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CMPDTA'.Compare Value
:LISTCOL VAR=START USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/START'.Compare Start
:LISTCOL VAR=RPYLONG USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/RPYLONG'.Reply
:LISTCOL VAR=DUMP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/DUMP'.Dump
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT SEQ MSGID RPY CMPDTA START'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT SEQ MSGID RPYLONG DUMP'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKRPYLH.Work with System Reply List Entries - Help
:P.The entries a job with INQMSGRPY(*SYSRPYL) consults before an
inquiry waits: the first whose message identifier and compare value
match answers it. F6 adds an entry, 2 changes one, 4 removes one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display, F5 reads the
list again, F11 shows each reply whole with the dump setting.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='WRKRPYLE/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SEQ'.Sequence Number
:P.The sequence Number of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGID'.Message ID
:P.The message ID of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RPY'.Reply
:P.The reply of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CMPDTA'.Compare Value
:P.The compare Value of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/START'.Compare Start
:P.The compare Start of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RPYLONG'.Reply
:P.The reply of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DUMP'.Dump
:P.The dump of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKRPYLE/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Reply List Entry (CHGRPYLE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Remove
Reply List Entry (RMVRPYLE) command is prompted for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
